---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Portrait from "../components/Portrait.astro";
import CtaLink from "../components/CtaLink.astro";
import { site, expertise } from "../site";
---

<Base title="About Blake Turner" description={`${site.owner}, a Charlotte native, owns Pixel & Tally and is the person you talk to. We build booking websites and dashboards for Charlotte restaurants and small businesses.`}>
  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
    <Portrait class="aspect-[4/5] w-full max-w-sm" />
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem)]">Meet the <span class="text-accent">owner.</span></h1>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>I'm {site.owner}. I grew up in Charlotte, NC and studied business and IT at NC State.</p>
        <p>
          Before Pixel & Tally I was a business operations analyst at Red Ventures, working for Fortune 500 utility
          clients. I wrote the SQL that pulled sales data out of several systems, cleaned and joined it, and fed the Tableau
          dashboards that sales directors used to run teams across four countries. I built the workflows and API
          connections that moved that data on its own, trained AI agents on real business data, and turned the numbers
          into insights leaders acted on every week.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before that I did data work at UNC Health and spent a summer in tax accounting at a Charlotte, NC CPA firm, so
          a P&L or a QuickBooks export reads like English to me.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now I wire small businesses together the same way. On sites we've built, Stripe holds a card until a detailer
          accepts the job, Twilio masks every call and text, a Google Shopping connection pulls store prices every Monday,
          the PSA API fills in a sports card from its cert number, and scheduled jobs email an owner her to-do list each
          morning. If your tools have an API, we can make them talk. If they only export a spreadsheet, we can work with that too.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started Pixel & Tally to bring that same work to local owners. Pixel is the website side. Tally is the numbers
          and automation. Most web shops can't build a dashboard, and most analysts don't build websites, so we do both.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every project starts with a call with me. I gather what you need, take it back, and we build it to fit. When you
          text, I'm the one who answers. There's no account manager and no one you get handed off to.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2 class="mt-12 text-3xl">What I'm good at</h2>
      <dl class="mt-5 divide-y-2 divide-dashed divide-hairline border-y-[3px] border-ink">
        {
          expertise.map((e) => (
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <dt class="font-mono text-sm font-bold uppercase">{e.area}</dt>
              <dd class="leading-relaxed">{e.detail}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <div class="sticker mt-10 bg-sunk p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm font-bold uppercase">Who I work with</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Owner-run restaurants, salons, barbers, detailers, cleaners, accountants, trades and studios, usually 1 to 20 people on staff.
          {site.serviceArea} That includes {site.areas.slice(0, -1).join(", ")} and {site.areas.at(-1)}.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <CtaLink href="/contact/">Book a free consult with me</CtaLink>
        {site.linkedin && <CtaLink href={site.linkedin} variant="ghost">LinkedIn</CtaLink>}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
